{"seq":18,"trial_id":"harness-zero-h2h-2026-11/hermes-opus-none-mu-v03-dev2/sy-02-marrow-fieldworks-ticket-numbers/r4","wall_ts":"2026-11-07T09:07:25.214Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"0bc9b6acdc5bb1f47d1527a17bdc651c347484e4c5760c15ea04b173a60f2ea8","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","text":"Here's what I found for Marrow Fieldworks. None of the notes name it outright next to a ticket, so I've said how I matched each one.\n\n1. #4409: from Moss's \"Central handoffs next week\" digest (teams/team-central/digests/2026-01-02-central-handoffs.md). It's a recurring timeout on the Gatehouse Check-In report at the Salina North yard (Bay 4 and the west grain-bin apron, during the 06:00 flatbed intake). Hollis flagged it as open on Pree's dealer account before Marrow Fieldworks changed hands on Mon 5 Jan 2026.\n2. #4412: same digest. It's a minor glitch in the driver SMS prompt when combine trailers are staged on unpaved overflow lots. It's also from Hollis's pre-handoff list.\n3. #8841: from #central-random, your message on 13 Oct at 09:27. West yard Door 2 at the Plains depots still double-books when flatbeds check in early at the kiosk. That was your reply to Hollis asking about the tractor-bay alerts on \"Tobias's dealer account\". I've taken that to be Marrow Fieldworks since it moved to you in the January handoff, but please confirm.\n\nLeft out:\n- FR-882 (same Moss digest) is a feature request from Marrow Agrisupply, which is a different account.\n- #4419 and #PD-4492 in Moss's North digests belong to Quarrendon Freight Lines.\n- Pree's IT/Okta ticket in #central-random isn't a customer ticket.\n\nThere are no account files (tickets/CRM) for Marrow Fieldworks in the share I can see, so this list only covers those notes and the channel.","thread_ts":"1791987000.000123"},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","ts":"1791987000.000124","thread_ts":"1791987000.000123"}}
{"seq":19,"trial_id":"harness-zero-h2h-2026-11/hermes-opus-none-mu-v03-dev2/sy-02-marrow-fieldworks-ticket-numbers/r4","wall_ts":"2026-11-07T09:07:32.283Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"5b7aa6b7bf13e748511c55435ae17ffc50e7ed20410c0155cf7d354fc56ec581","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","text":"I found three ticket numbers that look like Marrow Fieldworks and sent you the list in our DM thread. Two of them depend on my guess about which account Moss and the channel mean, because no note names Marrow Fieldworks next to a ticket number.\n\n- **#4409** is from Moss's \"Central handoffs next week\" note (2 Jan 2026). It's a recurring timeout on the Gatehouse Check-In report at the Salina North yard, at Bay 4 and the west grain-bin apron during the 06:00 flatbed intake. Hollis flagged it as open on Pree's dealer account before Marrow Fieldworks changed hands on 5 Jan.\n- **#4412** is from the same note. It's a minor glitch in the driver text-message prompt when combine trailers are staged on unpaved overflow lots.\n- **#8841** is from your own message in #central-random on 13 Oct at 09:27, about West yard Door 2 double-booking when flatbeds check in early. You were answering Hollis's question about \"Tobias's dealer account\". I took that to mean Marrow Fieldworks, since it moved to you in January. Please check that's right.\n\n**Left out:**\n- FR-882 is a feature request from Marrow Agrisupply, which is a different account.\n- #4419 and #PD-4492 belong to Quarrendon Freight Lines.\n- Pree's login ticket with IT isn't a customer ticket.\n\nThis only covers Moss's notes and #central-random. I couldn't see any Marrow Fieldworks ticket or CRM files in the shared drive, so there may be others."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","ts":"1791987000.000125"}}
